# Line-ending policy.
#
# This working tree lives on a Windows path (C:\code\ai-note-taker) and is
# accessed by BOTH Git for Windows (system autocrlf=true) and Git inside WSL
# (autocrlf unset, i.e. false). Without a fixed policy the two disagree: one
# checks out CRLF, the other flags every line as changed — producing phantom
# whole-file diffs that show in one tool but not the other.
#
# Forcing LF in the index AND the working tree keeps both Gits in agreement.
# `text=auto` lets Git auto-detect binary files and leave them untouched.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Common binary assets — never normalize or diff as text.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.ico  binary
*.svg  text eol=lf
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.pdf  binary
